{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Under Rule 6c-11(d), the ETF must preserve:\n\n- **AP agreements:** Each written agreement between the ETF (or its service provider) and an authorized participant that allows the AP to place creation or redemption orders, including all amendments.\n- **Basket records:** For each day, the basket exchanged with each AP in creation and redemption transactions, including the identity and quantity of each basket holding. Keep records of any custom basket, along with the detailed parameters used in constructing it and the revisions to those parameters.\n\nKeep these records **for at least five years**, with the **first two years in an easily accessible place**. The rule’s exact language is “readily accessible” for that initial two-year period."}}
